#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-AD0225 expect=noViolation domain=ADLBC
#note "THE BASE COLUMN IS ABSENT. BASE != 0 is true over the all-missing fold, but the arithmetic conjunct resolves BASE to no vector and returns an empty set, so the rule executes and is silent. Pins finding AD0225-F1 (the shipped expression carries NO derived var_exists(\"BASE\") in front of BASE != 0, and none is owed because the arithmetic half supplies the polarity). Mirrors sibling PMDA-AD0225A's own valid_base_absent fixture, which reaches the same verdict by the other route."
#library standard=adamig version=1-3
#expectViolationCount 0
dataset ADLBC structure=BDS
col STUDYID type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col PARAMCD type=Char
col AVAL    type=Num
col PCHG    type=Num
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | ALB | 12 | 25
